course: dictionary
lesson: 15849
title: Undyed: the colour that is already there
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from parts you already know. Undyed is made of un- and dyed. Un- means not, and dye is a liquid or powder used to change the colour of cloth, wool or cotton. So undyed means not coloured with dye.
explain: «The shop sold undyed wool, so every ball was the natural colour of the sheep.» The sentence does not say the colour, but the clue is natural colour. Undyed wool still looks the way it looked when it came off the sheep.
explain: Look for undyed in art lessons, textile lessons and science lessons. Artists and designers often start with undyed cotton or wool, and they add colour later. Eco-friendly clothes are often made from undyed fibres, because no dye is added.
fact: Undyed means not coloured with dye.
fact: Undyed materials keep their natural colour.
fact: The un- at the start means not, so undyed is the opposite of dyed.
fact: Undyed is used about materials such as wool, cotton and yarn.
fact: A shop might label wool undyed to show it is plain and natural.
exercise: «The shop sold undyed wool, so every ball was the natural colour of the sheep.» What does undyed mean? | *Not coloured with dye, still its natural colour | Bright red and blue | Made from plastic | Dyed twice to be extra strong
exercise: «The art class used undyed cotton for the first sketches.» Which word from the sentence tells you the cotton had no colour added? | first | *undyed | sketches | class
exercise: Why would a shop label its wool as undyed? | *To show the wool is plain and natural, with no dye added | To show it has been dyed three times | To show it is made from plastic | To show it is wet from the rain
test: «Eco-friendly clothes are often made from undyed fibres.» What does undyed tell the reader about the fibres? | The fibres are broken | The fibres are very old | *The fibres are plain and natural, with no dye added | The fibres are bright and colourful
test: Which of these is undyed? | Scarf dyed bright pink | Jumper dyed green | Wool dyed deep blue | *Cotton still in its natural cream colour
exam: «The undyed yarn was the colour of oatmeal.» What does undyed mean? | *Not dyed, so still its natural colour | Stretched and broken | Dyed black | Sold in a bag
